      "side": 1,
      "message": "Unfortunately `-C clusterx.has_arm_v9-0\u003d1` does not automatically enable BTI simulation in the FVP (even though Armv9 architecture makes BTI mandatory). So we will need to add the `-C clusterx.has_branch_target_exception\u003d1` FVP parameter here explicitly.\n\nI was able to verify this locally. I disabled `-Zbranch-protection\u003dbti` for the stdlib build. Then with the `-C cluster0.has_arm_v9-0\u003d1` parameter alone, everything unexpectedly works fine. Adding `-C clusterx.has_branch_target_exception\u003d1` to the FVP command line makes the boot fail \"properly\" (it hangs after printing `INFO: Setting MMU config`).",
